           "longComment": "Cooper was able to play all 72 of the team's defensive snaps in Sunday's 20-17 overtime win against the Jets, recording eight total tackles (six solo), including 1.0 sacks, in the contest. The Packers didn't hold an official practice Monday, but the linebacker's ability to be considered limited is a positive sign for his chances to play Thursday night versus Atlanta."
