           "shortComment": "Briningstool caught his only target for nine yards and made two tackles in Monday night's 31-10 win over the Broncos.",
           "longComment": "Briningstool played 13 of 69 offensive snaps primarily as a blocker for Kenneth Walker. The tight end's bigger role came on special teams, where he played 20 snaps and made a tackle in kick coverage and punt coverage. Briningstool's success comes after No. 4 tight end Jared Wiley was inactive as a healthy scratch, further showing Briningstool's place on the tight end totem pole."
