        "637599": {
         "recordId": "637599",
         "athleteName": "Maxx Crosby",
         "positionAbbr": "DE",
         "teamId": "13",
         "teamAbbr": "LV",
         "teamName": "Las Vegas Raiders",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-26T08:09:09.681Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-27T02:40:21.775Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-16T03:17Z|Crosby had two tackles (one solo) and 1.5 sacks in Sunday's 27-13 win over the Dolphins.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-16T03:17Z",
           "shortComment": "Crosby had two tackles (one solo) and 1.5 sacks in Sunday's 27-13 win over the Dolphins.",
           "longComment": "Crosby didn't do much in the first three quarters of the contest, though it was a different story in the fourth quarter, with the veteran accounting for 1.5 of the Raiders' 5.0 sacks on the day. It was an interesting offseason for Crosby, who was nearly traded to Baltimore. He also underwent surgery to repair a torn meniscus in his left knee. However, Crosby looks to be back at full strength, and he appears more motivated than ever, which isn't good news for opposing offenses."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638352": {
         "recordId": "638352",
         "athleteName": "Tre Tucker",
         "positionAbbr": "WR",
         "teamId": "13",
         "teamAbbr": "LV",
         "teamName": "Las Vegas Raiders",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-26T08:09:09.681Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-27T02:40:21.775Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-21T00:20Z|Tucker caught five of seven targets for 119 yards and a touchdown in the Raiders' 26-14 win over the Chargers on Sunday.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-21T00:20Z",
           "shortComment": "Tucker caught five of seven targets for 119 yards and a touchdown in the Raiders' 26-14 win over the Chargers on Sunday.",
           "longComment": "With Brock Bowers (knee) missing a second straight game to open the season, Tucker matched Ashton Jeanty with a team-high seven targets against Los Angeles, and the speedy wideout got free behind the defense for a 40-yard score to open the scoring in the second quarter. One of the more boom-or-bust receivers in the sport, Tucker now has seven grabs for 146 yards and the one touchdown on 11 targets through two games to begin the 2026 campaign. He'll be in position for another big performance next Sunday in the Superdome against the Saints."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638356": {
         "recordId": "638356",
         "athleteName": "Ashton Jeanty",
         "positionAbbr": "RB",
         "teamId": "13",
         "teamAbbr": "LV",
         "teamName": "Las Vegas Raiders",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-26T08:09:09.681Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-27T02:40:21.775Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-21T00:28Z|Jeanty rushed 21 times for 48 yards and brought in four of seven targets for 15 yards in the Raiders' 26-14 win over the Chargers on Sunday.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-21T00:28Z",
           "shortComment": "Jeanty rushed 21 times for 48 yards and brought in four of seven targets for 15 yards in the Raiders' 26-14 win over the Chargers on Sunday.",
           "longComment": "Jeanty was the unquestioned leader of the Raiders' ground attack once again, and although he had to scratch and claw for every yard, the second-year back helped keep the Bolts' defense honest. Jeanty also finished second in receptions and tied for the team lead in targets, underscoring how central he is to what Las Vegas does on offense. Jeanty and his teammates will be gunning for a third consecutive victory to open the season when they tangle with the equally surprising Saints on the road next Sunday."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638382": {
         "recordId": "638382",
         "athleteName": "Kirk Cousins",
         "positionAbbr": "QB",
         "teamId": "13",
         "teamAbbr": "LV",
         "teamName": "Las Vegas Raiders",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-26T08:09:09.681Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-27T02:40:21.775Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-21T01:37Z|Cousins completed 19 of 29 passes for 253 yards with three touchdowns and one interception while rushing four times for one yard in the Raiders' 26-14 win over the Chargers on Sunday.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-21T01:37Z",
           "shortComment": "Cousins completed 19 of 29 passes for 253 yards with three touchdowns and one interception while rushing four times for one yard in the Raiders' 26-14 win over the Chargers on Sunday.",
           "longComment": "Cousins' crisp and nearly mistake-free performance was critical to the Raiders pulling off a significant upset over their divisional rival. The veteran signal-caller validated head coach Klint Kubiak's decision to open the season with him as the starter over first overall pick Fernando Mendoza, with Cousins delivering a 40-yard strike to Tre Tucker in the first quarter and 13- and 11-yard scoring tosses to Cody White in the third and fourth quarters, respectively. Cousins has shown very good command of Kubiak's offense over the first two games, and he'll take a 67.8 percent completion rate and a 6:3 TD:INT into an intriguing interconference road matchup against the Saints next Sunday."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638411": {
         "recordId": "638411",
         "athleteName": "Michael Mayer",
         "positionAbbr": "TE",
         "teamId": "13",
         "teamAbbr": "LV",
         "teamName": "Las Vegas Raiders",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-26T08:09:09.681Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-27T02:40:21.775Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-21T03:32Z|Mayer brought in three of four targets for 23 yards in the Raiders' 26-14 win over the Chargers on Sunday.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-21T03:32Z",
           "shortComment": "Mayer brought in three of four targets for 23 yards in the Raiders' 26-14 win over the Chargers on Sunday.",
           "longComment": "Mayer served as the No. 1 tight end for the second straight game to open the season due to Brock Bowers' (knee) absence. Mayer played a complementary and mostly short-area role as expected, but through his two starts, he's posted a serviceable a 9-55-0 line on 11 targets. Bowers reportedly could be healthy enough to play in a Week 3 road matchup against the Saints, a development that would relegate Mayer to his usual No. 2 role."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638419": {
         "recordId": "638419",
         "athleteName": "Mike Washington Jr.",
         "positionAbbr": "RB",
         "teamId": "13",
         "teamAbbr": "LV",
         "teamName": "Las Vegas Raiders",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-26T08:09:09.681Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-27T02:40:21.775Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-21T04:03Z|Washington rushed three times for seven yards while failing to catch his only target during Sunday's 26-14 win over the Chargers.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-21T04:03Z",
           "shortComment": "Washington rushed three times for seven yards while failing to catch his only target during Sunday's 26-14 win over the Chargers.",
           "longComment": "Washington was far less efficient with his carries in Week 2, averaging 2.3 YPC after he turned seven carries into 41 yards against the Dolphins in the team's regular-season opener. The running back operated as a distant No. 2 option in the backfield, as Ashton Jeanty logged 21 carries for 48 yards while catching four of seven targets for 15 yards. Washington is nothing more than a bench stash option in fantasy leagues at the moment."
          }
         ]
        },
        "638420": {
         "recordId": "638420",
         "athleteName": "Jalen Nailor",
         "positionAbbr": "WR",
         "teamId": "13",
         "teamAbbr": "LV",
         "teamName": "Las Vegas Raiders",
         "history": [
          {
           "captured_at": "2026-09-26T08:09:09.681Z",
           "last_seen_at": "2026-09-27T02:40:21.775Z",
           "fp": "Active|2026-09-21T04:06Z|Nailor caught one of three targets for nine yards in Sunday's 26-14 win over the Chargers.",
           "status": "Active",
           "date": "2026-09-21T04:06Z",
           "shortComment": "Nailor caught one of three targets for nine yards in Sunday's 26-14 win over the Chargers.",
           "longComment": "Nailor's three targets were fourth on the team, and he continues to run plenty of routes. The production is lacking through two games, as Nailor has just four catches for 36 scoreless yards on eight targets. Cody White secured a pair of touchdowns as the fourth wideout Sunday, and it will be interesting to see if White starts getting more snaps at Nailor or Jack Bech's expense."
          }
         ]
        },
